{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Features for a Free Online HTML Editor"}, {"type": "position", "content": 5}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 3}, {"type": "level", "content": "A1.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when you talk about HTLM online editors. "}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe common simple incidents at work in a simple spoken or written situation with a supportive interlocutor. Represent the solution outline to the problem presented by the customer through making case of use diagrams, facing the problem to the customer following rules and protocols of the organization."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation. Exchanges simple information on programming tools and solutions to a client's requirement."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n2le03ob05re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Modal Verb Can for Ability: Interrogative Statements"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You usually use the <span class=\"italic\"> modal verb can </span> when you are referring to the abilities or functions of someone or something."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<p>Another structure using the modal verb <strong><i>can</i></strong> to talk about abilities is <strong><i>can + be + past participle</i></strong> of the main verb. You can use this structure when the subject of the sentence (the one doing the action) is implicit, not mentioned or when it&rsquo;s not necessary to mention it. &nbsp;Look at the examples:</p> <p>Emphasis on the subject (Active):</p> <ul> <li>People <strong><i>can make</i></strong>&nbsp;websites online.</li> <li><strong><i>Can</i></strong> people <strong><i>make</i></strong> websites online?</li> </ul> <p>Emphasis on the object (Passive):</p> <ul> <li>Websites <strong><i>can be made </i></strong><i>online.</i></li> <li><strong><i>Can </i></strong>websites <strong><i>be made</i></strong> online?</li> </ul>"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":1,\"columns\":1,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<p><strong><em>Modal Verb Can in Passive Statements</em></strong></p>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\"\"}"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":6,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"> <span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Modal verb </span> </div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"> <span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Object </span> </div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"> <span class=\\\"strong\\\"> BE </span> </div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"> <span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Past participle of the verb </span> </div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"> <span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Complement </span> </div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"> <span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Interrogative </span> </div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<b>Can\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"websites\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<b>be\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<b>made\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"online?\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Can this editor be downloaded?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Can a website be made with a free online editor?"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "There is and There are to Talk About Features in an Online HTML Editor"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When you want to express the idea of the existence of something or you need to describe the features of an object, you can use the structures <span class=\"italic\"> <b>there is</b> </span> and <span class=\"italic\"> <b>there are</b>. </span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "There are many free online HTLM editors that offer different interactive features for website developers."}, {"type": "example", "content": "There are many services such as syntax highlighting, indentation, HTML cleaning and file conversion."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Absolutely, there is generally an option in which an invalided code can be fixed."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<p>You use <strong><i>there is</i></strong> to refer to singular or uncountable nouns, and <strong><i>there are</i></strong> to refer to plural nouns:</p> <ul> <li><strong><i>There is</i></strong> <strong>an HTLM source code editor</strong> on the right side of the page.</li> <li><strong><i>There are</i></strong><strong> different kinds of features</strong> in the control panel.</li> </ul> <p>You can make the forms <strong><i>there is</i> </strong>and <strong><i>there are</i></strong> negative by only adding the word <strong><i>not </i></strong>after the <strong>verb to be</strong>, or by contracting the verb to be combined with the word not: <strong><i>isn&rsquo;t</i></strong> or <strong><i>aren&rsquo;t.&nbsp;</i></strong></p> <ul> <li><strong><i>There isn&rsquo;t</i></strong> an HTLM source code editor on the right side of the page.</li> <li><strong><i>There aren&rsquo;t</i></strong> different kinds of features in the control panel.</li> </ul> <p>The interrogative form used to ask for details in the information is:</p> <ul> <li><strong><i>Is there</i></strong> an HTLM source code editor on the right side of the page?</li> <li><strong><i>Are there</i></strong> different kinds of features in the control panel?</li> </ul>"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "html cleaning "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a tool to correct HTML source code."}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: There are many services such as syntax highlighting, indentation, HTML cleaning and file conversion."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le03ob05aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": " file conversion "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an application to transform different types of file formats into html source code."}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: There are many services such as syntax highlighting, indentation, HTML cleaning and file conversion."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le03ob05aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "failing "}, {"type": "definition", "content": " a weakness of something."}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The only failing in this editor is the absence of a Lorem-Ipsum generator. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le03ob05aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "lorem-ipsum generator "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a tool that simulates possibilities of text layout in a website."}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The only failing in this editor is the absence of a Lorem-Ipsum generator."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le03ob05aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "bro